MS5837 — VENDORED, NOT A lib_deps DEPENDENCY
============================================

Upstream: robtillaart/MS5837 (see library.json for the version this was taken from).
Vendored 2026-08-02. `robtillaart/MS5837` was removed from platformio.ini's lib_deps in the
same commit — having both would make which copy compiles depend on LDF precedence, which is
exactly the kind of ambiguity this file exists to remove.

WHY IT IS VENDORED
------------------
The upstream `reset()` contains a real bug that silently corrupts every reading:

    uint32_t start = millis();
    while (micros() - start < 10) { ... }

micros() is ~1000x larger than a millis() baseline, so the condition is false on its first
evaluation and the loop body NEVER RUNS. The mandatory ~2.8 ms post-RESET PROM-reload delay
was therefore zero, and initConstants() read the calibration PROM in a race with the sensor
reloading it. Whether the coefficients came back intact was timing luck at every boot.

A corrupted C5 (Tref) of ~42220 instead of ~26646 reports -160 C. ~27833 reports +10 C. An
intact read reports correctly. That is the "sometimes -160, sometimes 10, sometimes perfect"
observed on the vehicle.

It is not only a temperature bug. dT feeds `offset` and `sens`, so a bad PROM corrupts
PRESSURE and DEPTH by a large, silent, sign-unpredictable amount. On a vehicle whose depth
loop has never run closed (AUDIT.md R1), that is the input the first closed-loop dive would
have been flying on.

The fix cannot live in src/drivers/bar30.cpp: the race is internal to reset() (RESET command
-> immediate initConstants()), C[] is protected, and there is no public seam to inject a
delay between the two. And a fix applied under .pio/libdeps is not a fix at all — that tree
is regenerated by any clean build, so it would reappear as "the temperature bug came back".

THE THREE DEVIATIONS FROM UPSTREAM
----------------------------------
Each is marked `SROT DEVIATION n of 3` in MS5837.cpp. If you re-vendor a newer upstream,
re-apply all three or re-open all of the above.

  1. reset()          millis()-vs-millis(), 20 ms wait (was micros()-vs-millis(), 0 ms).
  2. reset()          validate the PROM's own CRC-4 and fail begin() when it does not match.
                      Upstream says "SKIP CRC check (for now)"; that comment is the bug's
                      last line of defence and it was switched off.
  3. read()           conversion wait `<= wait` rather than `< wait`. millis() ticks at an
                      arbitrary phase, so `< wait` can exit ~0.2 ms in at OSR 8 and readADC()
                      then returns 0 or the previous conversion while reporting success.

Plus: promCrcOk() / promRaw() are new public methods, MS5837_ERROR_CRC (-12) is a new error
code, and _temperature/_pressure are now initialised (they were uninitialised members read
across calls).

This follows the same convention as lib/mavlink/ — see lib/README.
